            <ArticleTitle>[Initial experiences with simultaneous combined radiation and cytostatic chemotherapy in the modification of intractable pain by inoperable tumor growth in the ENT area].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>136-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Patients with malignant tumours of the ENT, who show signs of tumour progression after operation, radiation and chemotherapy, could be treated with a new combined therapy. We present a patient who was successfully treated by combined radiation and chemotherapy with Cisplatin, Ifosfamid, and BCNU. This therapy offers a chance of tumour reduction even for repeatedly treated patients. The relief of pain proves the success of the therapy.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
